# The M9 sim's walk over the fixture (1530): a board without a client
# record, as it comes off the flasher. Run by `just m9-sim-walk`, grammar in
# loquax-m9/src/bin/loquax-m9-sim/script.rs; every dump is for the eye.

# The pairing, then Back to the fixture's list.
dump 00-pairing.png
back
dump 01-chats.png

# A chat, scrolled back by a held ring up, and left.
down
down
enter
dump 02-chat.png
hold up 1000
dump 03-chat-scrolled.png
back

# The map: its words stand by the clock, then T and Y.
map
dump 04-map-open.png
wait 7000
dump 05-map.png
t
dump 06-map-t.png
y
dump 07-map-y.png

# The bubbles back to the list, the square bubble to compose, a line typed.
f1
f3
text Hallo M9
dump 08-compose.png
back

# The house key (1532, 1561): a press opens the settings at once (the
# controller repeats no held key, so there is no hold to wait for). Left
# steps the type's value, Enter confirms it: very small. Right twice and
# Enter: large. A step Back drops keeps the size; Back again closes.
home
dump 09-house.png
left
dump 09-house-stepped.png
enter
dump 09-house-tiny.png
right
right
enter
dump 09-house-large.png
left
back
back
dump 09-chat-large.png
# Enter steps round the values from large to very small, Enter confirms.
home
enter
enter
dump 09-chat-tiny-house.png
back
dump 09-chat-tiny.png
home
right
enter
back
dump 09-chat-small.png

# Every screen the goldens pin, through the board's FRAME_DUMP path.
screen chats 10-chats.png
screen chat 11-chat.png
screen groups 12-groups.png
screen invite 13-invite.png
screen members 14-members.png
screen admin 15-admin.png
screen ask 16-ask.png
screen pick 17-pick.png
screen name 18-name.png
screen map 19-map.png
screen pan 20-pan.png
screen pairing 21-pairing.png
